WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.755
Narrator: As far as supervillains go,

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:06.280
Thanos is, well, not very bright.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.320
Say what you will about Doc Ock,

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.070
Syndrome, or Lex Luthor.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.870
At least they put considerable

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.584
scientific thought
behind their evil plans.

00:00:14.584 --> 00:00:17.520
Nanowires feed directly
into my cerebellum.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.330
Narrator: Meanwhile, check
out Thanos' master plan.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.820
The entire time I knew Thanos,

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.060
he only ever had one goal:

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.610
to bring balance to the universe

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.120
by wiping out half of all life.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.810
Narrator: Yeah, this scheme
to conserve resources

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:38.350
by eliminating half of
all life makes no sense.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.340
In fact, it wouldn't save the planet.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.473
It would doom it.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.640
Let's start with his decision
to wipe out half of humanity.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.060
Now at first, you can see his reasoning.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.950
After all, there are 7.7 billion
humans on the planet today.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.700
That's nearly 7% of all the people

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.210
who have ever lived in the
history of our species,

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.000
which makes for a pretty crowded planet.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.630
So if half of us suddenly vanished,

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.590
wouldn't that be a worthy sacrifice?

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.760
No. Ethics aside, we'd still be left

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.850
with almost 3.9 billion people,

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:24.380
about the same world population in 1972.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.550
So if history repeats itself,

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.770
it would buy us less than 50 years

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.090
before we reached current levels again,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.320
and the same is true
for many animal species

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.750
like deer, whose healthy populations

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.600
would help them rebound quickly.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.420
But unfortunately, the same can't be said

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:45.300
for endangered species who
have the opposite problem.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.070
Take the critically endangered
Sumatran tiger, for example.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.920
Experts estimate there are fewer

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.320
than 400 left on the planet.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.460
If half disappeared, there wouldn't be

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.660
enough to sustain the population,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.530
and they would likely go extinct,

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.090
and endangered sharks, hawks, and leopards

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.030
would probably meet the same fate,

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:08.060
and that's where Thanos' plan to save

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.880
the world really falls apart.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.140
Once a top predator disappears,

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.680
they can take the rest of
their ecosystem down with them.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.930
Take gray wolves for example.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.990
The US government eradicated them

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.370
from Yellowstone in the 20th century.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.910
With the wolves gone, the elk population

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.250
exploded and devoured
the local vegetation,

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.310
which disrupted the population of

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.420
beavers, birds, and other species

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.690
that relied on those plants to survive,

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:38.490
and it gets even worse once you consider

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:42.120
that half of every plant
species on Earth is gone too

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.130
because just like with animals,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.320
there are thousands of
endangered plant species,

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.610
many of which are too vulnerable

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.900
to survive Thanos' plot,

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.930
and if plant species die out,

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.500
the rest of their food chain would starve.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.820
Of course, many plant
populations aren't endangered,

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.700
but even that won't save
them all in the long run.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.520
You see, scientists
estimate that 90% of all

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.000
flowering plants depend
on animals to reproduce,

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.440
but Thanos wiped out half of all

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:16.000
bees, fruit bats, and every
other pollinator on the planet,

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.610
many of which are already in trouble.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:22.660
For example, 50% of bee
species in the Midwest

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.950
have vanished in the past century,

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.850
and the lesser long-nosed bat,

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.360
a key pollinator in the Sonoran desert,

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.060
is also disappearing,

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.210
so they would probably die off completely,

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:36.850
and if enough pollinators go poof,

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:41.710
we're looking at a possible
total ecological collapse.

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:44.560
So while Thanos' plan wouldn't

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.690
directly devastate thriving species,

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.360
the chain reaction that could come

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.860
from eliminating endangered species

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.376
could really mess things up
for everyone else left alive.

00:03:55.376 --> 00:03:57.590
No resurrections this time.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.840
Narrator: Nice going, Thanos.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.570
To be fair, the planet has experienced

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:06.040
mass extinctions before,
and life recovered.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.510
For example, an asteroid
strike 66 million years ago

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:14.590
wiped out 75% of all species on Earth,

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:16.800
and with the dinosaurs out of the way,

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.690
our mammalian ancestors flourished.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.340
But even so, experts estimate it takes

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:24.980
around 20 million to 30 million years

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.170
to recover from a mass extinction.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:29.480
So unless waiting around for millennia

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.405
was all part of the plan,

00:04:31.405 --> 00:04:34.893
the Mad Titan messed up, big time.

